 ## Rental module
 
 `createRentalService()` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns an in-memory service with
-`addEquipment`, `quote`, `book` and `availability`. Run the tests with `npm test`.
+`addEquipment`, `quote`, `book`, `availability` and `cancel`. Run the tests with `npm test`.
 
 - Money is an integer number of euro cents; `total` is `dailyPrice` times the number of days; a rental of 3 days or more gets 10% off that
   full price, rounded to the nearest cent. `quote` and `book` both return the reduced total.
@@ -22,4 +22,8 @@ of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
 - `availability({ start, end, kind? })` returns the sorted ids of the items, of that kind or of any kind when
   none is given, that are free for the whole period (same period rules as `quote`).
 - Invalid input, unknown items and clashing bookings throw an `Error`.
-- Cancellation (no refund under 24 hours before the start, full refund otherwise) is not implemented yet.
+- `cancel(bookingId, at)` cancels a booking at the instant `at` (ISO-8601 UTC, any time of day) and returns
+  `{ bookingId, refund }`. The refund is the full booking total when `at` is at least 24 hours before the
+  start, and 0 when it is later (including after the start). A cancelled booking no longer holds its
+  equipment, and a booking can be cancelled only once. An unknown booking, a second cancellation or an
+  invalid `at` throws an `Error`.
